{
 "ep": 10,
 "total": 140,
 "title": "psql: The Essential PostgreSQL Command-Line Tool",
 "phase": "Foundations",
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Five psql commands every DBA should know.",
   "cap": "Five *psql* commands every DBA should know."
  },
  {
   "say": "This is episode ten of the PostgreSQL DBA series. Today: connect, explore a database, and get help in psql.",
   "cap": "Episode 10: *connect,* *explore,* get *help.*",
   "cue": "explore"
  },
  {
   "say": "psql is the interactive terminal for PostgreSQL. You type a query, and psql sends it to the server.",
   "cap": "psql sends your *SQL* to the *server.*",
   "cue": "server"
  },
  {
   "say": "Anything starting with a backslash is a meta-command, handled by psql itself.",
   "cap": "*Backslash* commands run inside *psql* itself.",
   "cue": "meta-command"
  },
  {
   "say": "To connect: psql, dash capital U postgres, dash d appdb.",
   "cap": "Connect: *-U* user, *-d* database.",
   "cue": "dash"
  },
  {
   "say": "No host given? psql uses a local Unix-domain socket. The server port is five four three two by default.",
   "cap": "No host: *Unix* *socket.* Default port *5432.*",
   "cue": "five"
  },
  {
   "say": "No user given? psql uses your operating system user name, and the same name for the database.",
   "cap": "Default user = *OS* *user.* Database = same name.",
   "cue": "database"
  },
  {
   "say": "Command one: backslash conninfo. It shows the database, user, socket and port. Check it before anything risky.",
   "cap": "1. *\\conninfo:* where am I connected?",
   "cue": "database"
  },
  {
   "say": "Command two: backslash L lists the databases, with owner and encoding. Output trimmed. Add a plus for sizes.",
   "cap": "2. *\\l* lists databases. *\\l+* adds sizes.",
   "cue": "owner"
  },
  {
   "say": "Command three: backslash du lists roles.",
   "cap": "3. *\\du* lists *roles.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "postgres is a superuser. app_user has no special attributes.",
   "cap": "*postgres:* Superuser. *app_user:* none."
  },
  {
   "say": "Command four: backslash d describes objects. backslash dt lists tables.",
   "cap": "4. *\\d* describes. *\\dt* lists tables.",
   "cue": "dt"
  },
  {
   "say": "backslash d orders shows columns, types, nullability and the primary key index.",
   "cap": "*\\d* *orders:* columns, types, *indexes.*",
   "cue": "columns"
  },
  {
   "say": "Command five: backslash x turns on expanded display.",
   "cap": "5. *\\x:* expanded display."
  },
  {
   "say": "Each column prints on its own line. Great for wide rows.",
   "cap": "*One* *column* per line."
  },
  {
   "say": "Forgot a command? backslash question mark lists them all.",
   "cap": "*\\?* lists every *meta-command.*",
   "cue": "question"
  },
  {
   "say": "backslash h DROP DATABASE shows the SQL syntax, with a link to the docs.",
   "cap": "*\\h* DROP DATABASE: SQL *syntax* help.",
   "cue": "syntax"
  },
  {
   "say": "Bonus: backslash timing shows each statement's time in milliseconds.",
   "cap": "*\\timing* shows time in *ms.*",
   "cue": "milliseconds"
  },
  {
   "say": "Start psql with dash capital E to see the real query behind each backslash command.",
   "cap": "*-E* shows the query behind *\\dt.*",
   "cue": "real"
  },
  {
   "say": "Common mistake: no semicolon. Nothing runs, and the prompt changes to dash hash.",
   "cap": "No *semicolon?* Prompt becomes *appdb-#.*",
   "cue": "prompt"
  },
  {
   "say": "psql is waiting for more. Type the semicolon, and it runs. Meta-commands need none.",
   "cap": "Type *;* to send it. Backslash needs none.",
   "cue": "semicolon"
  },
  {
   "say": "DBA takeaway: read your prompt. A hash means a superuser. A greater-than sign means a normal user.",
   "cap": "*#* superuser. *>* normal user.",
   "cue": "greater-than"
  },
  {
   "say": "On a hash prompt, slow down: every command runs with full power.",
   "cap": "On *#,* every command has *full* *power.*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Recap: conninfo, L, du, d and x.",
   "cap": "Recap: *\\conninfo,* *\\l,* *\\du,* *\\d,* *\\x.*",
   "cue": "du"
  },
  {
   "say": "And backslash q quits psql.",
   "cap": "*\\q* quits psql."
  },
  {
   "say": "Next up: the PostgreSQL configuration files. Follow so you don't miss it, and send this to a friend who's learning PostgreSQL.",
   "cap": "Next up: *config* *files.* *Follow* and share."
  }
 ],
